  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Rain moves out of the region this evening.\n\nLow pressure will track front Ohio into Pennsylvania through this \nevening. The back edge of steadier rain will move out of the region \narea by mid afternoon. A few showers will be possible through the \nevening after the steadier rain tapers off. Low level moisture \nwill remain high through tonight, mist and/or drizzle will be \npossible for at least the first half of the night tonight. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Chances for showers and thunderstorms return \nThursday through the weekend.\n\nThe pattern will become active again starting Thursday as a mid \nlevel wave drops through a broad longwave trough and pushes a \nweak cold front into the region. Moisture returning on the back \nside of departing high pressure will support showers and possible\nthunderstorms as the cold front moves through on Thursday. \nAdditional, but lower chances for showers and thunderstorms will\ncontinue into the weekend as several ill-timed shortwave move \nthrough the region.",
